# Milestone: M5
# Covers: at.sync (obj.x.changed?) — synchronous slot-change subscriber;
#         body runs inline before the slot-write statement returns; value
#         visible to subscriber is the new value just written.
#
# blocked: at.sync syntax not implemented
# matrix-row: reactive-slot-change
#
# Reason:
#   Same blockers as slot_change_basic.chk.  The sync (AT_SYNC) vs async (AT)
#   mode distinction for slot-change watchers is documented in spec #4 §5.3 and
#   tested in test_slot_change_reentrancy.c at the C level.
#
# Activate when Object.new() + slot-change scripted subscribe + inline dispatch wired.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T69 + M5-scratch-frame):
#   var obj = Object.new();
#   var seen = 0;
#   at.sync (obj.x.changed?) Realm.seen = obj.x;
#   obj.x = 7;
#   seen
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000000] nil
#   [00000001] 0
#   [00000002] nil
#   [00000003] 7
#   [00000004] 7
